The C++ Vulkan runtime is newly written; its device/queue and graph resource
design references the pinned upstream runtime. Shader modifications are described
in scripts/prepare_shaders.py and the source/modification summary below.

The C++ ONNX reader adapts the bounded protobuf-reader design and normalization
from lxw112190/SimdPaddleOCR, Apache-2.0, commit
d94a79ec56ec0d9bec1cb7c45f91dc1081161080. The unmodified OnnxProtoReader.cs snapshot
is retained under third_party/simd-paddleocr/onnx-reference. LayerNorm/attention
and register-tiled pointwise shaders reuse the earlier pinned upstream kernels.
PP-OCRv6 Tiny/Small/Medium ONNX assets follow the official PaddlePaddle model
sources listed in docs/ONNX-MODELS.md and models/onnx/catalog.json.

nlohmann/json is distributed under its MIT license.
PP-OCRv6 model assets retain their upstream attribution and Apache-2.0 license.

BGR recognition preprocessing is adapted from lw.PPOCR.C (MIT),
Copyright (c) 2026 天天代码码天天. Its complete MIT license is included at
licenses/lw-PPOCR-C-MIT.txt. Reviewed source revision:
b7d2b42383adcee68b0e4f1a7c3de546be9c9552.
DB postprocessing, DET preprocessing, perspective cropping and reading order
also reuse lw.PPOCR.C MIT sources; CLS preprocessing and portable bitmap adapters
are derived implementations. Reduced private headers are provided for this port.
The C++ DET preprocessing fast path also adapts that MIT implementation,
hoisting horizontal resize coordinates while preserving its double-precision
interpolation/normalization operation order. Buffer upload/readback memory
selection and persistent mapping are project-written Vulkan runtime changes.
The CLS/REC coordinate-hoisting implementation and channel-shared perspective
crop in src/crop_optimized.c also adapt the same pinned MIT lw.PPOCR.C sources;
the unmodified reference sources and full MIT license are retained.

The C++ split/coalesce lifetime planner is inspired by MIT lw.PPOCR.C
src/runtime/memory.c. Graph-level shared grow-only workspace and lazy rebinding
reference the pinned upstream Vulkan arena design. The new FP32 register/shared-memory
GEMM kernels and affine/ReLU graph optimizer are project-written implementations.
Kernel-major FP32 vector depthwise convolution, timestamp diagnostics and guarded
HardSwish/SiLU graph fusion are also project-written additions.
Guarded exact-pattern GELU lowering, FP32 GELU epilogues and transpose-convolution
bias/activation fusion are project-written. The M64/N64 pointwise experiment is
also project-written and remains a default-off engineering option.
The separately gated experimental cooperative-matrix GEMM follows the pinned
upstream subgroup/shared-staging design; its FP32-buffer / mixed-FP16 port,
tile layout and capability checks are newly written. It is not a release default.

HTTP support uses cpp-httplib 0.49.0 (MIT), spdlog 1.17.0 (MIT) and its
bundled fmt 12.1.0 (BSD-2-Clause), copied from the author's lw.PPOCR.OpenCVDNN
repository. Service scripts are adapted from that project (Apache-2.0).
cpp-httplib has a documented local transport queue-overflow 429 patch.
stb_image 2.30 is pinned at 2c980bb59875b0d32144a71867fbdebb2f77cd20,
from https://github.com/nothings/stb; used under the included MIT alternative.

Source repositories and modification summary
------------------------------------------
Shader/runtime design reference: https://github.com/sdcb/SimdPaddleOCR,
feature/2.0, commit 6298596e28404f0e93af585a79e84086363eeb72 (Apache-2.0).
ONNX reader reference: https://github.com/lxw112190/SimdPaddleOCR,
commit d94a79ec56ec0d9bec1cb7c45f91dc1081161080 (Apache-2.0).
Host geometry/preprocessing reference: https://github.com/lxw112190/lw.PPOCR.C,
commit b7d2b42383adcee68b0e4f1a7c3de546be9c9552 (MIT).

Unmodified shader snapshots under third_party/simd-paddleocr/shaders include
conv_dense, conv_dw, convt2s2, elem, reduce_hw, resize4, concat_c, maxpool4,
nchw2nhwc, avgpool4, softmax, attn and layernorm, from the pinned upstream
src/Sdcb.SimdPaddleOCR/Backends/Vulkan/Shaders directory. Build-time variants
remove FP16 extensions/types, retain NHWC scheduling, use FP32 HardSigmoid
parameters, improve Erf precision and use an FP32 MaxPool lower bound.
Generated variants identify their modifications; original snapshots remain.
The pointwise convolution adapts the conv1x1_dot register-tile math with tails
and without optional fused operands. Project-written FP32 tiled GEMM,
parallel Softmax/argmax, epilogues and vector depthwise additions are separate.

The native ONNX port retains bounded protobuf child messages and adapts
Identity/metadata normalization and exact LayerNorm/QKV-attention recognition.
It adds graph/constant/string budgets and strict canonical-layout checks.
Offline CLS/REC lowering turns inference BatchNormalization into channel
scale/bias and constant tail MatMul into transposed-weight 1x1 convolution.
Arbitrary Transpose/Reshape are not silently treated as no-ops.
Resource wrappers use official Vulkan headers and explicit RAII ownership.
Shape plans use a bounded 32-entry LRU and shared arena/IO; cached command
references are invalidated before buffer replacement and lazily rebound.

Unmodified host snapshots include db_postprocess.c, det_preprocess.c, crop.c,
reading_order.c and the crop/reading-order headers in third_party/lw-ppocr-c.
Private compatibility headers are not the complete upstream SDK. Scalar
bitmap adapters replace AVX2 dependencies and use four orthogonal neighbors;
the upstream scalar tail used a different diagonal approximation. Profiling
is disabled in this extraction. Derived CLS/REC preprocessing retains double
interpolation order, bounded aspect-preserving resize and padding. Native CTC
is project-written with the same greedy semantics and dictionary indexes.
The local optimized perspective crop shares sampling coordinates across
B/G/R without changing pixel math; the original crop is retained for tests.
Host reference tests share this geometry; they are not an independent DB
algorithm implementation. Golden geometry tests cover its basic contracts.

Optional cooperative-matrix code references conv1x1_cm_sg32 shared staging,
subgroup32 and FP32 accumulation, but uses FP32 global buffers and K-major
weights rather than the upstream FP16/N-major layout. It remains separately
gated and default-off; upstream accuracy, speed and compatibility are not
inherited or claimed. Models retain the official sources and licenses listed
in docs/ONNX-MODELS.md. Reuse does not imply endorsement by upstream authors.
